  "notes": "ぶらつく is an informal verb describing aimless wandering or hanging around. It comes from the onomatopoeia ぶらぶら (dangling, swinging loosely), suggesting a relaxed, unhurried movement.\n\nRelated expressions:\n- ぶらぶらする: similar meaning, to loaf around\n- {散歩|さんぽ}する: to take a walk (more purposeful)\n\nWhile often neutral, ぶらつく can have slightly negative connotations when describing someone who should be doing something productive.",
